ba349",26,-1,1,"nit: can you expand on this description (in particular mentioning what the behavior is with the flag disabled)."],["32094dec_5a6c2b0e",5,-1,0,"Is there a risk that in future the `OnChange` implementation might assume `env` is non-null? At a minimum can we add a warning comment to the method definition. I'd prefer exposing a separate method…"],["866f2a6e_fdcf3f5e",5,-1,1,"Same as above."],["918eb2ea_8a2a93de",25,-1,1,"nit: I don't think exposing this via a method helps readability or maintainability - prefer to read the flag directly from call sites."]],0,445],[7229085,20427,395,8.956,7.286,[[1,0.604,179,239],[0,0.333,175,132],[7,0.063,15,25]],[["ef195d2d_95485fe6",50,0,1,"nit and optional: I wonder if its worth adding android to the name of this test suite? I was a quite confused as to how FakeContentFiltersObserverBridge was able to be included here until i scrolled…"]],0,446],[7236487,20433,279,10.07,8.247,[[0,176]],[["e75c0ea8_c8c018a1",51,0,1,"optional nit / maybe follow-up: check that `SetUpBrowserContextKeyedServices` has not been called yet? Otherwise it seems like a common way to not have the thing working as expected Or maybe only…"]],0,447],[7259234,20437,354,10.07,8.247,[[0,0.994,177,351],[28,0.006,47,1]],[["3414b62f_4cfae92b",52,0,0,"Question: It looks like the test is not being run on ChromeOS at all, would it make sense to just not include it in the crosOS build?"],["a68d5229_a4dfc499",53,0,1,"Question: what is does ACP stand for here? if its AndroidParentalControlsState could you clarify in this comment? something like`ACP(AndroidParentalControlsState) browser filter state`"],["de2e0353_09236a9f",54,0,1,"Could you please either remove this class or add tests that use it to this CL?"]],0,448],[7251354,20439,458,10.07,8.247,[[0,0.483,178,228],[1,0.221,180,97],[9,0.211,31,98],[4,0.037,54,16],[29,0.026,8,11],[7,0.01,16,4],[11,0.006,34,2],[8,0.006,5,2]],[["028ca19b_ade525aa",6,-1,1,"Is this the correct bug? It doesn't seems to mention why we need this change."],["2098ecd7_b0f95c30",55,-1,1,"can you register the factory? https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:ios/chrome/browser/profile/model/keyed_service_factories.mm;l=374"],["474166c9_d8556a37",6,-1,0,"I don't quite understand why this is needed as a separate service. I agree with the separation though as sus is very bloated. Is SUS no longer created for users with supervision enabled by android?…"],["e7ade1b7_20112d2c",56,-1,1,"I think we should also update chrome/browser/profiles/chrome_browser_main_extra_parts_profiles.cc"],["f9dd9e44_3e63ac01",55,-1,1,"can you add a TODO?"],["fb433717_143fd29e",57,-1,1,"Could you reference a bug here to make sure its tracked?"],["3a5e8c32_4cc27407",56,0,1,"nit: per comment on line 212, this should go earlier in the list"]],0,449],[7260485,20439,172,5.298,4.261,[[1,0.743,181,128],[0,0.213,179,37],[9,0.044,32,7]],[["39812fc3_7ef811a0",58,-1,1,"Nit: typo ```suggestion {\"WithSupervisedUserUrlFilter\", true}, ```"],["56425c21_19f408da",58,-1,1,"Nit: typo ```suggestion {\"WithSupervisedUserUrlFilter\", true}, ```"],["9328566f_2469d2dd",58,-1,1,"For simplicity, should we use \"base::test::WithFeatureOverride\" instead? https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:base/test/with_feature_override.h Otherwise, the label should be more…"]],0,450],[7265331,20439,109,3.575,2.85,[[1,0.843,182,96],[0,0.132,180,11],[7,0.025,17,2]],[["1db2b855_e23475b9",6,0,1,"made"]],0,451],[7277818,20445,491,8.956,7.286,[[1,0.673,183,337],[0,0.229,181,108],[11,0.069,35,33],[7,0.025,18,12],[2,0.004,9,1]],[["04f38b20_1ff7e0f4",5,0,0,"What is the logic behind adding this extra check here? It looks like this is related to the removed condition in `ContentFiltersObserverBridge::SetEnabled()` but there is no…"],["056c70a3_0351b020",7,0,1,"typo: sounds like a verb is missing? ```suggestion // \"this instance\" is const (e.g. when used in KeyedServiceFactory). ```"],["06911cc9_ee445f0e",2,0,1,"nit: could these two be made non ptr types? I see that they are built unconditionally and are never reset manually. ```suggestion FakeContentFiltersObserverBridge…"],["095039e5_9a97b09b",59,0,1,"nit: can be `const` (as const pointers) Also, I think we could directly use raw pointers here and document the requirement that content filter observers must outlive this service (they currently do…"],["0bbaef78_61b8c53a",60,0,1,"optional: This feels a little bit too heavy for a factory singleton initialization to my taste. I don't have a very good intuition about how much time the Java-side initialization is going to take…"],["19e57c31_5d0c2e37",61,0,1,"optional: crash immediately if this is null ```suggestion CHECK_DEREF(supervised_user::AndroidParentalControlsServiceFactory::GetForProfile( profile)) ```"],["24a36567_45a2a91b",12,0,1,"nit: comment got truncated"],["3adcfcbb_a7045b34",59,0,1,"Will these signals differ from profile to profile? As of now, `AndroidParentalControlsService` doesn't have any dependency on `Profile` so it might be a singleton as well."],["402e029c_385bc063",7,0,1,"nit: this comment is still not right ```suggestion // container with known secure settings. Instances of // FakeContentFiltersObserverBridge for testing purposes are available // from…"],["48e1cc8d_a3756f18",53,0,1,"nit: It looks like these methods might be no longer needed. `SetEnabledForTesting()` can be called directly on a factory and you've also migrated off calling `IsEnabled()` directly on the filters."],["492d33d6_6370fe4a",62,0,0,"nit: could this be moved outside of the `*Core()` function to `PostBrowserProcessInit()` above? I think this function is supposed to be collapsed into `PostBrowserProcessInit()` when some testing…"],["4b1ef4c7_c274c7ed",5,0,1,"naming nit: `any_local_parental_control_enabled` or `any_content_filters_enabled` sounds like a better fit to separate this from family link parental control. ```suggestion bool…"],["5b0d1618_011da04a",5,0,1,"nit: please consider using `base::ScopedObservation` (best practice)"],["698655c3_fc41543f",63,0,1,"nit: the destructor of a derived class should be marked override ```suggestion ~AndroidParentalControls() override; ```"],["7b5bc323_6546e11e",64,0,1,"nit: swap these two to keep an alphabetical order ```suggestion #if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) supervised_user::AndroidParentalControlsServiceFactory::GetInstance(); #endif…"],["7f4117aa_2636acc0",4,0,1,"drive-by, optional: this class has lots of logging that is discouraged in Chromium unless you are tracking down a specific bug Consider removing logging statements or at least converting them to…"],["92db8382_eeb37901",5,0,1,"nit: please avoid using the same histogram logging call in multiple places. How about a helper function to record this histogram?…"],["9a3d8434_907ccea7",53,0,1,"nit: can be moved to the .cc file"],["b41afe0b_e7058eda",65,0,1,"Please add unit-tests for this file."],["bb796e9e_0700d790",63,0,1,"nit: this method is not implemented, please remove"],["c5aded4d_15d54f4e",7,0,1,"drive-by nit: looks like a leftover ```suggestion // Instances of FakeContentFiltersObserverBridge for testing ```"],["c94e3d09_0141f53c",10,0,1,"nit: for consistency ```suggestion ASSERT_FALSE(GetAndroidParentalControls() ```"],["cd709fa8_8d286a93",65,0,1,"nit: please use `base::ScopedObservation` to de-register observers automatically."],["d3f5a44e_02ae68b8",60,0,0,"As an opposite of prescription profiles? Anyways, shouldn't we rather use `supervised_user::BuildProfileSelectionsForRegularAndGuest()` for profile selection here?"],["daceb57a_609cc8f4",7,0,1,"nit: no longer needed?"],["f0392081_73e588ba",65,0,1,"nit: Is this even needed? `AndroidParentalControlsService` is created with zero observers and it won't be possible to register an observer until the object is constructed."],["fe4fade4_b45922a0",66,0,1,"nit: can this just be a member of the test fixture class (like in `chrome/browser/metrics/family_link_user_metrics_provider_unittest.cc`)?"]],0,452],[7287701,20446,113,3.575,2.85,[[1,0.902,184,102],[0,0.098,182,11]],[],0,453],[7287433,20446,82,3.042,2.433,[[0,0.822,183,71],[1,0.178,185,11]],[["1523bc6e_165a1d8f",67,0,0,"Noting for a later CL: I think it would be good to consider having a client / delegate abstraction like GetDeviceParentalcontrols() or similar instead of GetAndroidParentalControls(). This would…"],["5ba6ce5a_c96ae2fe",6,0,1,"nit: did you mean for apc to be a topic (I don't think adding it with # here does anything)?"]],0,454],[7320460,20446,17,0.939,0.709,[[1,186]],[],0,455]]}